.\"	$GergiOS$
.Dd July 5, 2026
.Dt IRQTOP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm irqtop
.Nd display per-IRQ thread statistics
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar delay
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl m Ar warn_max
.Op Fl n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
displays real-time statistics for per-IRQ kernel threads.
Each IRQ vector is serviced by a dedicated ring 0 kernel thread
running at SCHED_FIFO priority.
Statistics are read from the kernel via
.Xr sys_getinfo 2
with
.Dv GET_IRQTHREAD_STATS .
.Pp
The columns are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "MAX_LAT"
.It IRQ
IRQ vector number (0\(en63).
.It NAME
Short descriptive name for the IRQ (timer, keyboard, serial, msix-N, ...).
.It PRIO
SCHED_FIFO real-time priority (1\(en99, higher = more urgent).
.It HANDLED
Total number of IRQ events handled.
.It RUN
Total number of times the handler was invoked.
.It LAST_LAT
Latency of the most recent handler invocation, in TSC ticks.
.It AVG_LAT
Average latency over all invocations, in TSC ticks.
.It MAX_LAT
Worst-case (maximum) latency observed, in TSC ticks.
.It REG
Whether an IRQ handler has been registered for this vector.
.El
.Pp
Latency is measured as the number of TSC (Time-Stamp Counter) ticks
between the moment the kernel signals the IRQ thread and the moment
the thread begins executing the handler.
To convert TSC ticks to nanoseconds, divide by the TSC frequency in MHz
(displayed in the summary line).
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d Ar delay
Set the refresh interval in seconds (default: 1.0).
.It Fl h
Display help text and exit.
.It Fl m Ar warn_max
Highlight rows whose MAX_LAT exceeds
.Ar warn_max
TSC ticks.
.It Fl n
One-shot mode: print statistics once and exit without clearing the screen.
Useful for scripting or non-interactive use.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag
.It Nm
Display statistics with a 1-second refresh.
.It Nm Fl d 0.5 Fl m 10000
Refresh every 500 ms, highlight IRQs with more than 10,000 ticks latency.
.It Nm Fl n
Print a single snapshot to stdout.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr top 1 ,
.Xr systat 1 ,
.Xr sys_getinfo 2
.Sh AUTHORS
.An GergiOS
